From 11ea271ab93db88665c5e6a1ca4c617e342e195e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:09:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Wake a manually activated DPMS on input as well

A display blanked through the ToggleDPMS builtin stays blank until the
same builtin runs again: WakeUpScreenSaverAndDPMS() refuses to touch a
manual DPMS state, so no key, button or remote press brings the picture
back. Meanwhile every one of those presses is handed to the GUI, which
acts on a screen nobody can see, and a media centre bound to a remote
has no way to tell the user which button is the one that returns.

Wake on input in that case too, passing the current mode to
ToggleDPMS() so the toggle is allowed to proceed, which also makes the
waking press be swallowed rather than acted upon.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 xbmc/application/ApplicationPowerHandling.cpp | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/xbmc/application/ApplicationPowerHandling.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/ApplicationPowerHandling.cpp
@@ -119,11 +119,9 @@ bool CApplicationPowerHandling::WakeUpSc
   // First reset DPMS, if active
   if (m_dpmsIsActive)
   {
-    if (m_dpmsIsManual)
-      return false;
     //! @todo if screensaver lock is specified but screensaver is not active
     //! (DPMS came first), activate screensaver now.
-    ToggleDPMS(false);
+    ToggleDPMS(m_dpmsIsManual);
     ResetScreenSaverTimer();
     result = !m_screensaverActive || WakeUpScreenSaver(bPowerOffKeyPressed);
   }
